Looking at this problem, I need to find the entry in the 8th row and 8th column of a grid where each entry (for i,j ≥ 2) equals the sum of all entries in the sub-grid above and to the left of it.

## Setup

Let $a_{i,j}$ denote the entry in row $i$, column $j$. We have:
- $a_{1,j} = 1$ and $a_{i,1} = 1$ for all $i, j$.
- $a_{i,j} = \displaystyle\sum_{r=1}^{i-1}\sum_{c=1}^{j-1} a_{r,c}$ for $i, j \geq 2$.

Define the 2D prefix sum $S(i,j) = \sum_{r=1}^{i}\sum_{c=1}^{j} a_{r,c}$. Then $a_{i,j} = S(i-1, j-1)$ for $i,j \geq 2$.

## Key Simplification

Using the standard prefix-sum identity:
$$S(i,j) = S(i-1,j) + S(i,j-1) - S(i-1,j-1) + a_{i,j}$$

For $i,j \geq 2$, substituting $a_{i,j} = S(i-1,j-1)$:
$$S(i,j) = S(i-1,j) + S(i,j-1) - S(i-1,j-1) + S(i-1,j-1) = S(i-1,j) + S(i,j-1)$$

This is the **Pascal recurrence**. The boundary values are:
- $S(1,j) = j$ (sum of $j$ ones in row 1)
- $S(i,1) = i$ (sum of $i$ ones in column 1)

## Closed Form

I claim $S(i,j) = \binom{i+j}{i} - \binom{i+j-2}{i-1}$.

**Boundary check:** $S(1,j) = \binom{1+j}{1} - \binom{j-1}{0} = (1+j) - 1 = j$. ✓  
$S(i,1) = \binom{i+1}{i} - \binom{i-1}{i-1} = (i+1) - 1 = i$. ✓

**Recurrence check:**
$$S(i-1,j) + S(i,j-1) = \left[\binom{i+j-1}{i-1} - \binom{i+j-3}{i-2}\right] + \left[\binom{i+j-1}{i} - \binom{i+j-3}{i-1}\right]$$
$$= \binom{i+j-1}{i-1} + \binom{i+j-1}{i} - \left[\binom{i+j-3}{i-2} + \binom{i+j-3}{i-1}\right] = \binom{i+j}{i} - \binom{i+j-2}{i-1} = S(i,j). \checkmark$$

## Computation

The desired entry is $a_{8,8} = S(7,7)$:

$$a_{8,8} = S(7,7) = \binom{14}{7} - \binom{12}{6} = 3432 - 924 = \boxed{2508}$$

## Verification (building the grid)

Using $a_{i,j} = S(i-1,j-1)$ and the recurrence, the full grid is:

| | c1 | c2 | c3 | c4 | c5 | c6 | c7 | c8 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| r1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 |
| r2 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 |
| r3 | 1 | 2 | 4 | 7 | 11 | 16 | 22 | 29 |
| r4 | 1 | 3 | 7 | 14 | 25 | 41 | 63 | 92 |
| r5 | 1 | 4 | 11 | 25 | 50 | 91 | 154 | 246 |
| r6 | 1 | 5 | 16 | 41 | 91 | 182 | 336 | 582 |
| r7 | 1 | 6 | 22 | 63 | 154 | 336 | 672 | 1254 |
| r8 | 1 | 7 | 29 | 92 | 246 | 582 | 1254 | **2508** |

**Spot-check $a_{5,5}$:** Sum of the $4\times 4$ sub-grid (rows 1–4, cols 1–4): $(1+1+1+1)+(1+1+2+3)+(1+2+4+7)+(1+3+7+14) = 4+7+14+25 = 50$. ✓

**Spot-check $a_{8,8}$:** Sum of the $7\times 7$ sub-grid = sum of row-sums (first 7 cols): $7+22+63+154+336+672+1254 = 2508$. ✓

